Keep the crash report in the database when a crash reporter is configured

The fork deletes the report as soon as a --crash-reporter is given, on the
assumption that the reporter reads the minidump back from the Sentry envelope it
also writes. Squey posts the minidump to BugSplat, which does not take that
format, so its reporter reads the report from the database instead: deleting it
leaves the reporter with nothing to send.

Note that the Linux version used the report ID after new_report had been moved
from by FinishedWritingCrashReport(), which this removes as well.

diff --git a/handler/linux/crash_report_exception_handler.cc b/handler/linux/crash_report_exception_handler.cc
index 11f0f47..2a6c198 100644
--- a/handler/linux/crash_report_exception_handler.cc
+++ b/handler/linux/crash_report_exception_handler.cc
@@ -328,7 +328,7 @@ bool CrashReportExceptionHandler::WriteMinidumpToDatabase(
   }
 
   if (has_crash_reporter) {
-    database_->DeleteReport(new_report->ReportID());
+    // The report is kept in the database for the crash reporter to pick up.
   } else if (upload_thread_) {
     upload_thread_->ReportPending(uuid);
   }
